!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Lung
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: 61
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = individual: ind_7
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = gender: male
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RNA sequencing was performed as previously described (Liu et al. 2016)  with slight modifications. Total RNA was extracted using Trizol reagent (Invitrogen).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For sequencing library construction, all samples were randomized first and prepared with TruSeq RNA Sample Preparation Kit (Illumina) according to the manufacturer’s instruction. Libraries were sequenced on the Illumina Hi-seq 4000 system in three lanes within one flow-cell, using the 150-bp paired-end module
!Sample_description = NA
!Sample_data_processing = Raw sequencing reads were filtered with Trimmomatic to remove adaptor content with parameters: PE ILLUMINACLIP: TruSeq3-PE-2.fa:2:30:1:0:8:true, SLIDINGWINDOW:4:15, MINLEN:25
!Sample_data_processing = Remaining high quality reads were aligned to reference genome GRCm38 using STAR-2.5.3 with parameters:  --sjdbOverhang 99 --outSAMattrIHstart 0 --outSAMstrandfield intronMotif --sjdbGTFfile GRCm38.gtf
!Sample_data_processing = Uniquely aligned reads were retrieved using: samtools -q 255
!Sample_data_processing = Expression levels were calculated as FPKM using cufflinks, yielding 51608 genes in total. Only the protein-coding genes were included in the analysis (using biotype feature of biomaRt) and the genes which are not detected (zero FPKM) in 25% or more of the samples (15/63) were excluded from the analysis, resulting in 15063 protein-coding genes in total.
!Sample_data_processing = FPKM values were 1+log2 transformed and quantile normalized using all the samples together.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCm38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: comma separated files contain ENSEMBL gene ids and normalized expression levels for each sample
